1
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:41,920
[Episode 26]

2
00:02:23,439 --> 00:02:24,760
Hello?

3
00:02:24,760 --> 00:02:26,639
<i>Qing Ye, it's me.</i>

4
00:02:26,639 --> 00:02:28,599
<i>My mom said you just had dinner with her.</i>

5
00:02:28,599 --> 00:02:29,885
<i>Are you back in Beijing?</i>

6
00:02:29,885 --> 00:02:32,262
Yes, I'm back.

7
00:02:32,262 --> 00:02:33,280
<i>Congratulations.</i>

8
00:02:33,280 --> 00:02:35,400
<i>Back to normal life.</i>

9
00:02:36,400 --> 00:02:38,439
Thanks.

10
00:02:38,439 --> 00:02:40,840
<i>Sounds like you're a little upset.</i>

11
00:02:40,840 --> 00:02:42,320
Really?

12
00:02:42,320 --> 00:02:43,719
Maybe

13
00:02:43,719 --> 00:02:46,520
I'm just a little out of place.

14
00:02:46,520 --> 00:02:47,800
<i>No way.</i>

15
00:02:47,800 --> 00:02:48,800
It's true.

16
00:02:48,800 --> 00:02:52,199
Zhazhating has not that many high-rises.

17
00:02:52,199 --> 00:02:54,247
Its lighting is not that good,

18
00:02:55,000 --> 00:02:58,360
and the air always smells like the sea.

19
00:02:58,360 --> 00:03:00,305
Logically,

20
00:03:01,120 --> 00:03:03,906
I should be happy to be back,

21
00:03:05,000 --> 00:03:07,000
but...

22
00:03:07,000 --> 00:03:09,319
<i>But you can't forget that place.</i>

23
00:03:15,040 --> 00:03:16,760
You're right.

24
00:03:39,400 --> 00:03:40,520
Wu!

25
00:03:40,520 --> 00:03:41,560
Dinner is ready.

26
00:03:41,560 --> 00:03:43,360
Come eat.

27
00:04:16,360 --> 00:04:18,199
<i>Hurry up, you're going to be late!</i>

28
00:04:18,199 --> 00:04:20,392
<i>Coming right here!</i>

29
00:04:23,720 --> 00:04:25,199
<i>I haven't done my hair yet.</i>

30
00:04:25,199 --> 00:04:26,839
<i>You'll be late in three minutes.</i>

31
00:04:26,839 --> 00:04:29,439
<i>If so, you are to be punished.</i>

32
00:04:29,439 --> 00:04:31,680
<i>- This will do.
- Quick!</i>

33
00:05:00,199 --> 00:05:02,920
I've been running around these days

34
00:05:02,920 --> 00:05:06,399
that I didn't take good care of Ye.

35
00:05:06,399 --> 00:05:08,560
She didn't even get to eat

36
00:05:08,560 --> 00:05:11,279
her favorite red bean zongzi.

37
00:05:11,279 --> 00:05:15,120
I thought she'd at least stay
through the Lantern Festival.

38
00:05:15,120 --> 00:05:17,959
Didn't expect her to leave in such a hurry.

39
00:05:23,319 --> 00:05:26,079
Why are you making such long faces?

40
00:05:26,079 --> 00:05:27,360
Ye

41
00:05:27,360 --> 00:05:30,040
is leaving our shabby nest

42
00:05:30,040 --> 00:05:33,120
for her golden one to enjoy life.

43
00:05:33,120 --> 00:05:36,279
That's a good thing. Why so unhappy?

44
00:05:39,040 --> 00:05:40,560
You're right.

45
00:05:40,560 --> 00:05:42,519
It's good.

46
00:05:42,519 --> 00:05:45,279
Without her,

47
00:05:45,279 --> 00:05:48,240
the house becomes empty and quiet.

48
00:05:48,240 --> 00:05:49,360
Well,

49
00:05:49,360 --> 00:05:51,240
people come, people go.

50
00:05:51,240 --> 00:05:53,439
It's like the four seasons.

51
00:05:53,439 --> 00:05:55,120
March brings peach blossoms and sunshine.

52
00:05:55,120 --> 00:05:56,319
That's wonderful.

53
00:05:56,319 --> 00:05:58,279
But it only lasts for a while.

54
00:05:58,279 --> 00:06:00,519
Summer is hot, winter is cold.

55
00:06:00,519 --> 00:06:02,519
You can't just dwell on the spring.

56
00:06:02,519 --> 00:06:04,643
Life has to go on.

57
00:06:05,519 --> 00:06:06,720
So,

58
00:06:06,720 --> 00:06:08,319
live today well,

59
00:06:08,319 --> 00:06:10,439
and spring will come again.

60
00:06:10,439 --> 00:06:11,680
The ones who leave

61
00:06:11,680 --> 00:06:14,079
will be seen again.

62
00:06:14,079 --> 00:06:15,519
Now eat.

63
00:06:29,600 --> 00:06:31,519
Finally home.

64
00:06:31,519 --> 00:06:32,879
The house is all cleaned up.

65
00:06:32,879 --> 00:06:34,399
The domestic helper is back, too.

66
00:06:34,399 --> 00:06:36,079
Just tell her if you need anything.

67
00:06:36,079 --> 00:06:38,120
Okay. Thank you, Uncle Sun.

68
00:06:38,720 --> 00:06:40,720
Ye is back! Welcome home.

69
00:06:40,720 --> 00:06:41,839
Come in. This way.

70
00:06:41,839 --> 00:06:43,000
Long time no see, Auntie.

71
00:06:43,000 --> 00:06:44,439
Come on.

72
00:06:46,620 --> 00:06:49,319
Okay. That's enough.

73
00:06:49,319 --> 00:06:50,680
Careful, it's hot.

74
00:06:50,680 --> 00:06:53,040
- Tell me when you're done.
- All right.

75
00:07:20,959 --> 00:07:23,082
<i>Is this one still alive? Look.</i>

76
00:07:23,840 --> 00:07:26,720
<i>Yes, it is. The Welwitschia is still alive.</i>

77
00:07:29,120 --> 00:07:30,160
Mom.

78
00:07:30,160 --> 00:07:31,439
Take this.

79
00:07:31,439 --> 00:07:32,920
What's this?

80
00:07:32,920 --> 00:07:34,600
My wages from this period.

81
00:07:34,600 --> 00:07:38,079
It's not much. Give it to Auntie Jin for rent.

82
00:07:38,079 --> 00:07:39,120
I have money.

83
00:07:39,120 --> 00:07:40,519
Keep yours.

84
00:07:40,519 --> 00:07:41,839
School is starting soon,

85
00:07:41,839 --> 00:07:43,879
and you'll need it for college later.

86
00:07:43,879 --> 00:07:44,959
Save it.

87
00:07:44,959 --> 00:07:46,680
Where did you get the money?

88
00:07:46,680 --> 00:07:48,040
When Qing Ye's dad left,

89
00:07:48,040 --> 00:07:49,720
he lent me some money.

90
00:07:49,720 --> 00:07:51,399
- 100,000 yuan.
- 100,000 yuan?

91
00:07:51,399 --> 00:07:52,920
I know what you're thinking,

92
00:07:52,920 --> 00:07:54,600
but it's not what you think.

93
00:07:54,600 --> 00:07:56,959
Don't worry. I didn't take advantage of him.

94
00:07:56,959 --> 00:07:59,959
I'm not that kind of person.

95
00:07:59,959 --> 00:08:02,560
He offered it on his own.

96
00:08:02,560 --> 00:08:04,959
He refused me to pay it back,
but I didn't agree.

97
00:08:04,959 --> 00:08:07,879
It's all there written down.

98
00:08:07,879 --> 00:08:10,160
However long it takes,
I'll pay it back in full.

99
00:08:10,160 --> 00:08:11,720
Don't worry.

100
00:08:12,519 --> 00:08:13,759
Then...

101
00:08:13,759 --> 00:08:15,720
does Qing Ye know?

102
00:08:17,839 --> 00:08:19,560
She probably does.

103
00:08:19,560 --> 00:08:21,079
I guess,

104
00:08:21,079 --> 00:08:23,937
she told her dad to do so.

105
00:08:26,519 --> 00:08:28,600
Look at them.

106
00:08:28,600 --> 00:08:29,759
100,000 yuan,

107
00:08:29,759 --> 00:08:32,559
handed over so easily.

108
00:08:32,559 --> 00:08:34,639
If it were the two of us,

109
00:08:34,639 --> 00:08:37,440
who knows how long we'd have to save?

110
00:08:37,440 --> 00:08:39,320
Worlds apart.

111
00:08:41,519 --> 00:08:43,240
Keep your money safe.

112
00:08:43,240 --> 00:08:45,269
Money isn't easy to come by.

113
00:08:53,840 --> 00:08:55,000
Ye,

114
00:08:55,000 --> 00:08:56,960
your dad went back to the company.

115
00:08:56,960 --> 00:08:59,320
He has a ton of things to deal with.

116
00:08:59,320 --> 00:09:00,320
School starts tomorrow.

117
00:09:00,320 --> 00:09:02,279
I'll come to take you in the morning.

118
00:09:02,279 --> 00:09:04,080
- Get some rest. I'll off.
- Okay.

119
00:09:04,080 --> 00:09:05,799
Goodbye, Uncle Sun.

120
00:09:31,919 --> 00:09:33,559
Mom.

121
00:09:34,200 --> 00:09:36,120
I'm home.

122
00:10:31,344 --> 00:10:32,768
[Search contacts: Xing Wu]

123
00:10:32,768 --> 00:10:34,621
[Contact not found]

124
00:10:50,292 --> 00:10:51,292
[Fuzz]

125
00:10:59,800 --> 00:11:03,907
[Qing Ye]
[Beijing]

126
00:11:56,240 --> 00:11:58,720
Only one semester left until Gaokao.

127
00:11:58,720 --> 00:12:00,399
We're in

128
00:12:00,399 --> 00:12:02,519
the home stretch now.

129
00:12:02,519 --> 00:12:05,120
I hope you can go all out

130
00:12:05,120 --> 00:12:06,279
to strive for

131
00:12:06,279 --> 00:12:08,600
the best future you can get.

132
00:12:09,919 --> 00:12:11,360
Let's begin.

133
00:12:28,400 --> 00:12:30,874
[High School English
Listening Intensive Training]

134
00:12:46,480 --> 00:12:48,240
Mom, how do you like the color?

135
00:12:48,240 --> 00:12:49,879
Thanks for your hard work.

136
00:12:49,879 --> 00:12:51,000
Here, have some water.

137
00:12:51,000 --> 00:12:52,509
Here.

138
00:12:52,509 --> 00:12:53,840
Sir. Here, have some water.

139
00:12:53,840 --> 00:12:55,727
Thank you.

140
00:12:57,680 --> 00:12:58,720
Grandma.

141
00:12:58,720 --> 00:13:01,240
Sir, have some water.

142
00:13:01,240 --> 00:13:02,799
Thanks.

143
00:13:03,679 --> 00:13:06,120
Sir, here, have some water.

144
00:13:06,120 --> 00:13:09,559
- Thank you. Have some water.
- Thanks.

145
00:13:30,399 --> 00:13:32,000
<i>It's alive, this Welwitschia.</i>

146
00:13:32,000 --> 00:13:33,919
<i>It's incredibly resilient.</i>

147
00:13:33,919 --> 00:13:36,840
<i>It can survive a long time in the desert.</i>

148
00:14:57,895 --> 00:15:01,574
[Countdown: 100 days to the Gaokao]

149
00:15:04,120 --> 00:15:05,679
Class, here are

150
00:15:05,679 --> 00:15:07,919
the 20 scoring points I've summarized.

151
00:15:07,919 --> 00:15:09,524
Memorize the steps.

152
00:15:09,524 --> 00:15:10,560
Later,

153
00:15:10,560 --> 00:15:12,560
once you're stuck on a similar problem,

154
00:15:12,560 --> 00:15:14,159
just plug in the steps.

155
00:15:14,159 --> 00:15:15,799
Remember, in math,

156
00:15:15,799 --> 00:15:17,799
even rote works if you stick to it.

157
00:15:17,799 --> 00:15:20,080
If you're unsure about a problem,

158
00:15:20,080 --> 00:15:21,200
don't leave it blank.

159
00:15:21,200 --> 00:15:22,759
Write as much as you can.

160
00:15:22,759 --> 00:15:26,279
Go over the vocab and grammar again,

161
00:15:26,279 --> 00:15:27,840
and cram as much as you can.

162
00:15:27,840 --> 00:15:30,085
Don't leave the long or short essay blank.

163
00:15:30,085 --> 00:15:33,279
Cram some phrases
to make sure you hit the word count.

164
00:15:33,279 --> 00:15:34,519
Use your time wisely.

165
00:15:34,519 --> 00:15:36,879
Last-minute prep is better than none.

166
00:15:36,879 --> 00:15:39,480
Grab every point you can.

167
00:15:43,159 --> 00:15:44,360
This is the last break

168
00:15:44,360 --> 00:15:46,039
before the final battle.

169
00:15:46,039 --> 00:15:47,600
You have three days.

170
00:15:47,600 --> 00:15:49,200
I want all of you

171
00:15:49,200 --> 00:15:50,960
to rest well

172
00:15:50,960 --> 00:15:52,639
and adjust your mindset.

173
00:15:52,639 --> 00:15:53,799
However,

174
00:15:53,799 --> 00:15:55,639
don't over-relax, either.

175
00:15:55,639 --> 00:15:58,519
We've worked hard for three years.

176
00:15:58,519 --> 00:16:00,039
I hope none of you

177
00:16:00,039 --> 00:16:02,447
leaves any regrets.

178
00:16:02,447 --> 00:16:04,039
Go all out for the exam.

179
00:16:04,039 --> 00:16:06,200
Go to your dream city.

180
00:16:06,200 --> 00:16:08,799
And get into your dream college.

181
00:16:08,799 --> 00:16:10,279
Good luck!

182
00:16:10,279 --> 00:16:16,257
- Good luck!
- Good luck!

183
00:16:18,279 --> 00:16:19,840
Where do you want to go?

184
00:16:19,840 --> 00:16:23,679
The provincial normal university.

185
00:16:23,679 --> 00:16:25,399
Closer to home.

186
00:16:30,000 --> 00:16:32,000
Wu, what about you?

187
00:16:47,960 --> 00:16:49,519
Beijing.

188
00:17:10,640 --> 00:17:12,125
Wu,

189
00:17:13,240 --> 00:17:15,119
call Grandma to eat.

190
00:17:15,119 --> 00:17:17,319
One more dish and it's ready.

191
00:17:19,079 --> 00:17:20,973
My son is the best.

192
00:17:21,599 --> 00:17:23,319
I love your attitude:

193
00:17:23,319 --> 00:17:25,578
so focused, forgetting to eat or sleep.

194
00:17:26,205 --> 00:17:28,039
Look at you.

195
00:17:28,039 --> 00:17:29,960
You're just like

196
00:17:29,960 --> 00:17:32,160
those ancient scholars studying for the exams.

197
00:17:32,160 --> 00:17:33,200
What was it called?

198
00:17:33,200 --> 00:17:35,720
"Hair to the beam and awl to the thigh."

199
00:17:35,720 --> 00:17:37,720
Is that how it goes?

200
00:17:37,720 --> 00:17:40,160
Yes, exactly.

201
00:17:40,160 --> 00:17:42,599
Alright. Go ahead. Call your grandma later.

202
00:17:42,599 --> 00:17:43,720
Take a break then.

203
00:17:43,720 --> 00:17:45,160
Okay.

204
00:17:52,559 --> 00:17:54,119
Grandma.

205
00:18:00,440 --> 00:18:02,039
Grandma.

206
00:18:05,519 --> 00:18:06,880
Grandma.

207
00:18:06,880 --> 00:18:08,359
Grandma.

208
00:18:09,240 --> 00:18:10,880
It's time to eat.

209
00:18:13,319 --> 00:18:15,400
Wu.

210
00:18:15,400 --> 00:18:17,279
I don't feel like eating.

211
00:18:17,279 --> 00:18:18,599
That won't do.

212
00:18:18,599 --> 00:18:20,000
You haven't eaten all day.

213
00:18:20,000 --> 00:18:21,359
Come on.

214
00:18:21,359 --> 00:18:23,039
I'll carry you downstairs.

215
00:18:29,440 --> 00:18:30,920
Come.

216
00:18:31,839 --> 00:18:33,319
Alright.

217
00:18:35,880 --> 00:18:38,160
Sorry for the trouble.

218
00:18:38,160 --> 00:18:39,880
I'm quite heavy.

219
00:18:39,880 --> 00:18:41,319
Lighter than a kitten.

220
00:18:41,319 --> 00:18:43,000
Time to eat!

221
00:18:46,799 --> 00:18:49,127
- Grandma, have some soup.
- Okay.

222
00:18:50,119 --> 00:18:54,119
Mom, at the rate Wu is going,

223
00:18:54,119 --> 00:18:56,519
he's bound to get into a top school.

224
00:18:56,519 --> 00:18:57,519
Here's the thing,

225
00:18:57,519 --> 00:19:00,578
our ancestors must be smiling down on him.

226
00:19:02,000 --> 00:19:04,920
Ye deserves the most credit.

227
00:19:04,920 --> 00:19:07,319
She talked Wu into returning to school.

228
00:19:07,319 --> 00:19:09,680
Yes, Grandma is right.

229
00:19:09,680 --> 00:19:11,680
But we still have to stay cool.

230
00:19:11,680 --> 00:19:14,039
I'll just do my best for the Gaokao,

231
00:19:14,039 --> 00:19:16,240
but I don't see myself entering a top school.

232
00:19:16,240 --> 00:19:17,599
I don't agree with that.

233
00:19:17,599 --> 00:19:19,319
Why not?

234
00:19:19,319 --> 00:19:21,400
You've got to think big.

235
00:19:21,400 --> 00:19:24,799
It gives you motivation.

236
00:19:24,799 --> 00:19:27,519
Your mom is right.

237
00:19:27,519 --> 00:19:30,640
I have great faith in you.

238
00:19:31,279 --> 00:19:33,519
Here. Have an egg.

239
00:19:33,519 --> 00:19:35,359
Full marks for the exam.

240
00:19:35,359 --> 00:19:37,039
Thank you, Grandma.

241
00:19:41,240 --> 00:19:43,720
Grandma, let me.

242
00:19:43,720 --> 00:19:45,319
Full marks for the exam.

243
00:19:45,319 --> 00:19:47,319
Mom, you have an egg too.

244
00:19:47,319 --> 00:19:48,680
Full marks for health.

245
00:19:48,680 --> 00:19:50,519
Good.

246
00:19:52,359 --> 00:19:54,171
Let me tell you some good news.

247
00:19:54,171 --> 00:19:55,640
Xuan Island is

248
00:19:55,640 --> 00:19:59,319
almost done with the renovation.

249
00:19:59,319 --> 00:20:02,039
After Wu's exams,

250
00:20:02,039 --> 00:20:03,720
I'll tidy up the shop.

251
00:20:03,720 --> 00:20:05,559
Then we can move back.

252
00:20:05,559 --> 00:20:06,680
Good.

253
00:20:06,680 --> 00:20:09,659
And I'm heading to the city

254
00:20:09,659 --> 00:20:11,880
for a nicer salon

255
00:20:11,880 --> 00:20:15,319
to brush up my skills.

256
00:20:15,319 --> 00:20:16,359
Everything will go well.

257
00:20:16,359 --> 00:20:19,200
Bad luck will go, and good luck will come.

258
00:20:20,200 --> 00:20:23,559
Grandma, things will get better.

259
00:20:23,559 --> 00:20:25,144
Good.

260
00:20:25,799 --> 00:20:28,799
Tomorrow is the fifteenth of the month.

261
00:20:28,799 --> 00:20:30,320
We should go

262
00:20:30,320 --> 00:20:32,920
worship the Dragon King and Mazu

263
00:20:32,920 --> 00:20:34,799
to fulfill our vows.

264
00:20:34,799 --> 00:20:37,724
Also, I want to watch the sunset.

265
00:20:38,519 --> 00:20:41,079
Great. I haven't gone out in a long time.

266
00:20:41,079 --> 00:20:42,680
I'll go with you.

267
00:20:42,680 --> 00:20:44,880
The forecast says heavy rain tomorrow.

268
00:20:44,880 --> 00:20:46,196
Maybe we should

269
00:20:46,196 --> 00:20:48,200
wait until the day after,

270
00:20:48,200 --> 00:20:50,559
- when it clears up?
- Good.

271
00:20:50,559 --> 00:20:51,559
It's settled.

272
00:20:51,559 --> 00:20:52,799
Good.

273
00:20:52,799 --> 00:20:54,400
Okay.

274
00:20:54,400 --> 00:20:56,640
The day after?

275
00:20:56,640 --> 00:20:58,788
The day after is fine.

276
00:21:00,400 --> 00:21:02,245
The day after is fine.

277
00:21:12,599 --> 00:21:14,070
Wu!

278
00:21:14,640 --> 00:21:16,096
Wu!

279
00:21:16,759 --> 00:21:18,640
Xing Wu!

280
00:21:21,599 --> 00:21:23,000
Xing Wu!

281
00:21:23,000 --> 00:21:24,759
Coming! I'm here!

282
00:21:26,920 --> 00:21:28,240
- Wu!
- What's wrong?

283
00:21:28,240 --> 00:21:29,759
I can't wake Grandma up.

284
00:21:29,759 --> 00:21:31,319
